:[0,0,0,0.0],"imax":[0,0,0,0.0],"streaming":[0,0,0,0.0],"dtc":[0,0,0,0.0],"ai_spend":[0,0,0,0.0],"tariffs":[7,7,0,17.25],"pricing_power":[0,0,0,0.0],"cost_cuts":[3,3,0,7.39],"guidance":[0,0,0,0.0,{"raise":0,"reaffirm":0,"cut":0}],"ai_disruption":[0,0,0,0.0]},"move":{"r1":0.0179,"r5":-0.0975,"r1_spy":0.0217,"r5_spy":-0.0903}}],"quotes":[{"c":"WHD 2018 Q4","e":"whd","d":"2019-03-07","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Brian Small","x":"…quarter represented approximately 26% of fourth quarter annualized revenues, slightly higher than in previous quarters due to the acceleration of inbound inventory shipments before the year-end with a view to minimizing we then expected by unrealized (ph) impact of additional Section 301 tariffs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/03/07/cactus-inc-whd-q4-2018-earnings-conference-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"WHD 2018 Q4","e":"whd","d":"2019-03-07","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Scott Bender","x":"Regarding tariffs, we have largely mitigated the impact of the Section 301 tariffs that were set at a rate of 10% on products imported from our wholly owned manufacturing subsidiary in China through a combination of factors discussed during our last call.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/03/07/cactus-inc-whd-q4-2018-earnings-conference-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"WHD 2019 Q1","e":"whd","d":"2019-05-02","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Scott Bender","x":"Further, we generated attractive margins despite lower commodity prices to start the year, rising costs associated with Section 301 tariffs and a strengthened Chinese currency in response to reduce trade tensions.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/02/cactus-inc-whd-q1-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WHD 2019 Q1","e":"whd","d":"2019-05-02","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Steve Tadlock","x":"Product gross margin at 39% was 170 basis points higher than Q1 2018, and 320 basis points lower sequentially due largely to the more fully realized impact of Section 301 tariffs and changes in FX rates, as Scott mentioned.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/02/cactus-inc-whd-q1-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WHD 2019 Q2","e":"whd","d":"2019-08-01","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Scott Bender","x":"Due largely to the impact of additional Section 301 tariffs, implemented in May, we expect product margins to be down low single-digit sequentially, less severe than we previously anticipated.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/01/cactus-inc-whd-q2-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WHD 2019 Q2","e":"whd","d":"2019-08-01","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Stephen Tadlock","x":"So I do think that we're handling the tariffs, I think much more effectively than our peers.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/01/cactus-inc-whd-q2-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WHD 2019 Q4","e":"whd","d":"2020-02-27","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Stephen Tadlock","x":"Product gross margins were relatively stable on a sequential basis at approximately 37% of revenues as the follow-through impact of Section 301 tariffs was less than expected.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/28/cactus-inc-whd-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WHD 2019 Q4","e":"whd","d":"2020-02-27","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Scott Bender","x":"Despite the increase in Section 301 tariffs to 25% that occurred in 2019 and overall market pressure during the latter part of the year, our product margins have continued to hold up well as previously mentioned.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/02/28/cactus-inc-whd-q4-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WHD 2020 Q1","e":"whd","d":"2020-05-01","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Stephen Tadlock","x":"Product gross margins were nearly 36% of revenues, down slightly on a sequential basis due to the full impact of Section 301 tariffs and the non-cash increase in our inventory obsolescence reserve.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/01/cactus-inc-whd-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WHD 2020 Q1","e":"whd","d":"2020-05-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Stephen Tadlock","x":"Given cost reduction measures implemented to date, we would expect SG&A to be $10 million to $11 million in Q2 2020, with stock-based compensation expense running at approximately $2 million during the quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/01/cactus-inc-whd-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WHD 2020 Q1","e":"whd","d":"2020-05-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Stephen Tadlock","x":"Due to headcount reductions announced in March, we recorded $1 million of severance expense in Q1 2020.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/01/cactus-inc-whd-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WHD 2020 Q2","e":"whd","d":"2020-07-30","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Stephen Tadlock","x":"Product gross margins increased to 36% of revenues, up 100 basis points on a sequential basis, in part due to $3.1 million in tariff-related benefits received during the quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/30/cactus-inc-whd-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WHD 2020 Q2","e":"whd","d":"2020-07-30","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Stephen Tadlock","x":"As disclosed in our release, Cactus recognized $7.5 million in refunds during the quarter associated with tariff exclusions granted in March of this year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/30/cactus-inc-whd-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WHD 2020 Q2","e":"whd","d":"2020-07-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Scott Bender","x":"Nonetheless we remain committed to further streamlining our existing operations, as we expect activity to remain below the levels needed to support the current industry capacity.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/30/cactus-inc-whd-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WHD 2020 Q2","e":"whd","d":"2020-07-30","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Stephen Tadlock","x":"We recorded just under $1 million of severance expense in Q2 2020.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/30/cactus-inc-whd-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"WHD 2020 Q3","e":"whd","d":"2020-11-05","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Scott Bender","x":"Our product EBITDA margins were expected to be in the low 30% during the fourth quarter, flat or slightly higher than our product EBITDA margins during the third quarter, excluding the impact of the 5.4 million arising from tariff refunds.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/11/06/cactus-inc-whd-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WHD 2020 Q3","e":"whd","d":"2020-11-05","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Stephen Tadlock","x":"And as far as tariff headwinds, I mean, last quarter, we said on an absolute worst-case scenario, if it didn't get extended, it would be 3% impact, and we noted 1% to 2% is more likely on an absolute basis.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/11/06/cactus-inc-whd-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WHD 2020 Q3","e":"whd","d":"2020-11-05","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Scott Bender","x":"Well, the easiest way to achieve it is to raise our prices, right?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/11/06/cactus-inc-whd-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WHD 2020 Q3","e":"whd","d":"2020-11-05","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Scott Bender","x":"And I don't see an opportunity to raise prices until -- I don't want to -- we never talk about prices on purpose, but there is no appetite for price increases right now.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/11/06/cactus-inc-whd-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WHD 2020 Q3","e":"whd","d":"2020-11-05","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Blake Gendron","x":"So you see it more as a revenue implication, building the moat, maybe getting some more market share on the rental side as opposed to we can streamline our costs, we can maybe rationalize the folks that are monitoring operations and with that sort of thing.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/11/06/cactus-inc-whd-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WHD 2020 Q4","e":"whd","d":"2021-02-25","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Stephen Tadlock","x":"Product gross margins were 31% of revenues, down approximately 1,400 basis points on a sequential basis due primarily to the Q3 impact of tariff refunds.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/25/cactus-inc-whd-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WHD 2020 Q4","e":"whd","d":"2021-02-25","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Stephen Tadlock","x":"Gross margins declined to negative 10% due to lower revenue on a relatively fixed depreciable base, a $600,000 decrease in tariff refunds and accelerated mobilization costs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/25/cactus-inc-whd-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WHD 2020 Q4","e":"whd","d":"2021-02-25","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Scott Bender","x":"So I think that the steel price increases that we're seeing, particularly in the Far East, the ocean freight increases that we're seeing, we will be able to offset with negotiations with those customers.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/25/cactus-inc-whd-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WHD 2020 Q4","e":"whd","d":"2021-02-25","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Scott Gruber","x":"Some color on your ability to pass it through to customers, whether that be a partial pass-through, a full pass-through.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/25/cactus-inc-whd-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WHD 2021 Q1","e":"whd","d":"2021-05-07","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Stephen Tadlock","x":"Product gross margins were 30% of revenues, down approximately 110 basis points on a sequential basis due primarily to increased costs associated with tariffs, materials, freight and wages.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/05/07/cactus-inc-whd-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WHD 2021 Q2","e":"whd","d":"2021-07-29","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Scott Bender","x":"That's not to say that the price increases were fully implemented by the end of June because they were not.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/29/cactus-inc-whd-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WHD 2021 Q3","e":"whd","d":"2021-11-04","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Chase Mulvehill","x":"And how easy is it for you to continue to push along price increases to offset kind of inflationary costs?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/04/cactus-inc-whd-q3-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WHD 2025 Q4","e":"whd","d":"2026-02-26","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Scott J. Bender","x":"The tariff environment as it applies to our imports to the U.S. had stabilized over the last several months, while future costs now appear to be trending down slightly but remain far from certain.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/26/cactus-whd-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WHD 2025 Q4","e":"whd","d":"2026-02-26","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Scott J. Bender","x":"To be clear, tariffs implemented under Sections 301 and 232 still total 75% on the majority of goods imported from China.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/26/cactus-whd-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WHD 2025 Q4","e":"whd","d":"2026-02-26","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Scott J. Bender","x":"The margin increase was due to a fuller benefit of cost reduction as compared to the third quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/26/cactus-whd-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WHD 2025 Q4","e":"whd","d":"2026-02-26","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Scott J. Bender","x":"…million in stock-based compensation, $3.3 million for transaction-related professional fees and expenses, $164,000 for additional restructuring actions to right-size the organization in response to the lower activity levels, and a $1 million loss related to the revaluation of the TRA liability.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/26/cactus-whd-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"WHD 2026 Q1","e":"whd","d":"2026-05-07","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Scott Bender","x":"I'd also like to provide a brief update on the tariff situation in the U.S. as it applies to our imports, which remain highly fluid.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/06/01/cactus-whd-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"WHD 2026 Q1","e":"whd","d":"2026-05-07","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Scott Bender","x":"We still pay a 75% total tariff on the import of most of our goods from China, which consists of 25% Section 301 and 50% Section 232.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/06/01/cactus-whd-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"WHD 2026 Q1","e":"whd","d":"2026-05-07","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Scott Bender","x":"They're always very reluctant to share that with us for fear that we're going to see that as an opportunity to raise prices, frankly.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/06/01/cactus-whd-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"WHD 2026 Q1","e":"whd","d":"2026-05-07","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jay Nutt","x":"…of $7 million in stock-based compensation, $10.4 million of inventory step-up amortization due to purchase price accounting, $5.8 million for transaction-relat